- ✅ `raw Blob as image input` → `OK image size=75 name=blob` (no regression).
- ✅ `video blob via handle_file` → `OK video size=2746 name=blob` — `handle_file(blob)` works in browsers (blobs have no filename, so the generic name is expected here; the size confirms the bytes arrived intact).

Fixes a cluster of `@gradio/client` packaging/distribution problems in `client/js`.

Closes #10028
Also fixes the CommonJS `require()` symptom reported in issue 9214 (gradio-app/gradio#9214 is **not** closed by this PR — its main "Could not resolve app config" bug is a separate problem).

### 1. Documented CDN bundle does not exist (#10028)

The README (and the gradio.app JS-client docs generated from it) tell users to load `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@gradio/client/dist/index.min.js`, but the package never shipped a `dist/index.min.js`. jsDelivr silently auto-minifies `dist/index.js` instead — the **Node** ESM build — so the documented `<script src=...>` snippet throws (classic script + `export` syntax), and even module imports get the wrong build.

**Fix:**
- New `bundle:cdn` build step (`BROWSER_BUILD=true CDN_BUILD=true vite build`) that emits a minified, single-file (`inlineDynamicImports`), browser-targeted ES module at `dist/index.min.js`, now part of `pnpm build`.
- README CDN snippet updated from the never-working bare `<script src=...>` form to the `<script type="module"> import { Client } from ... </script>` form that the guides already use (a bare classic script tag can never consume an ES module, and the docs' primary usage is the named `import`).

### 2. No CommonJS entry (`require("@gradio/client")` fails — symptom from #9214)

The package is `"type": "module"` and the exports map had no `require` condition, so `require("@gradio/client")` from CommonJS Node code resolves to ESM and throws `ERR_REQUIRE_ESM` on Node versions without `require(esm)` support (Node 18 / < 20.19 / < 22.12 — the package declares `engines.node >= 18`). This is why the reporter of #9214 needed the `new Function('modulePath', 'return import(modulePath)')` workaround.

**Fix:** the Node bundle step now also emits a CommonJS build at `dist/index.cjs`, wired up via a `require` condition in the exports map (plus `main`/`module`/`types` top-level fields and a `types` export condition).

